\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Definition}
\title{Reference-volume Jacobian}
\date{2026-11-10}

\p{Let #{T:X_V\to X_W} be an invertible real linear map between
finite real field spaces with their counting inner products #{h_V,h_W}.
Use its \vocabk{adjoint for chosen perfect pairings}{fdip-001P}
#{T^\dagger:X_W\to X_V}, characterized by
##{h_V(x,T^\dagger y)=h_W(Tx,y).}
The \newvocab{reference-volume Jacobian} is
##{J(T)=\sqrt{\det(T^\dagger T)},}
where the determinant is that of the endomorphism #{T^\dagger T} of
#{X_V} and the square root is the nonnegative real one.}
\p{The [counting dualities](fdip-001F) supply the adjoint.
The equivalence with the absolute top-form coefficient and the resulting
change of measure are \ref{fdip-002K}, using the convention of
\citet{Exercises 1.2.20-1.2.22, p. 41, preliminary version}{tao2011measure}.}
